    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-049: Text Align & Spacing (Measured, Deferred)**. **Decision record, no implementation.**\n\n**This is the first ADR in the session with `Status: Deferred` and no implementation branch.** The measurement is the deliverable.\n\n## Why deferred\n\nMeasurement on Wikipedia CSS (2026-10-29):\n\n| Property | Uses | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `letter-spacing` | **0** | Nothing to implement |\n| `word-spacing` | **0** | Nothing to implement |\n| `text-align: left` | 9 | No-op (default) |\n| `text-align: start` | 2 | No-op (left in LTR) |\n| `text-align: center` | 9 | Second-viewport or empty |\n| `text-align: right` | 5 | Second-viewport |\n| `text-align: justify` | 1 | **`@media print` only** |\n\nThe single `justify` rule is print-only, confirmed by 4 independent signals:\n- `pt` units (12pt/16pt body text)\n- `page-break-after: avoid`\n- `120pt` width\n- Surrounding context is all print typography (18pt/14pt/12pt headings)\n\n**Zero first-viewport targets. Zero scroll-verifiable targets before the first article table or figure.**\n\n## Why this differs from ADR-047 / ADR-048\n\n| ADR | Shipped? | Consumer |\n|---|---|---|\n| ADR-047 (mask-image) | Yes (paint code) | **Specific verified** — 3 `.vector-icon` in `display:none` ancestors, activate on ADR-029 |\n| ADR-048 (flex-wrap) | Yes (layout code) | **Specific verified** — `.mw-header` in HTML + viewport < 1680px |\n| **ADR-049 (text-align)** | **No** | **No identified future consumer** |\n\nADR-047 and ADR-048 shipped code because a *specific, verified* future consumer existed. ADR-049 has no such consumer — the properties are absent or print-gated in the target page.\n\n## What would reactivate ADR-049\n\nDocumented explicitly:\n1. A target page uses `letter-spacing` / `word-spacing` on first-viewport elements\n2. Wikipedia changes `p { justify }` to top-level or `@media screen`\n3. A future ADR renders print output (`@media print` reaching cascade)\n4. A specific first-viewport element needs `text-align: center|right`\n\n## Implementation sketch (for future reference)\n\nDocumented in the ADR, ~150-250 lines:\n- **Parse**: nothing (cascade already stores all properties)\n- **Line-fragment**: `TextAlign` enum + fragment field + justify needs word-boundary tracking\n- **Spacing**: `TextMeasurer` signature change (+2 params) + ~10 call sites updated + Pango attributes\n\nThe `TextMeasurer` signature change is the bulk of the cost and why `letter-spacing`/`word-spacing` aren't shipped speculatively.\n\n## The sixth verification category\n\nADR-049 establishes a new category in the session's decision ledger:\n\n| Category | Example | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| PNG-verified (first-viewport) | ADR-042, ADR-043 | visible delta |\n| PNG-verified (scroll) | ADR-045 | scroll delta |\n| Behaviorally-complete, visually-subtle | ADR-044 | shipped |\n| Behaviorally-complete, visually-zero | ADR-047, ADR-048 | shipped, consumer pending |\n| Deferred with reason | ADR-041 Commit 2 | specific step deferred |\n| **Measured, no target, deferred (this ADR)** | **ADR-049** | **no code** |\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 611 / 2386 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/049-text-align.md` — status Deferred; no implementation branch.\n\nRefs #229\n",
